---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Mineral Rights Scenario Calculator · MRX"
  description="Explore royalty income assumptions and compare a written offer per net mineral acre. Free educational calculator with transparent formulas and a human-review next step."
  path="/mineral-rights-calculator/"
  pageCategory="mineral-calculator"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Scenario Calculator', path: '/mineral-rights-calculator/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="container calculator">
    <p class="mrx-eyebrow">Free companion to your mineral-rights offer guide</p>
    <h1>Understand the numbers behind an offer.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An offer is built on assumptions. Explore how income, decline, timing and risk affect a
      scenario, then see which facts need a closer look before you sign.
    </p>
    <p>
      This calculator shows arithmetic using your inputs. It does not determine market value, verify
      ownership or produce an appraisal. MRX provides education only and does not buy mineral
      rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/before-you-sell-mineral-rights/">Get the free book and fillable worksheets</a> · <a
        href="/book/">Prepare a human underwriter conversation</a>
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="income-heading">
      <p class="mrx-eyebrow">For interests already paying royalties</p>
      <h2 id="income-heading">Model a producing-income scenario.</h2>
      <p>
        Use an average of representative royalty statements paid to you, after statement deductions.
        Exclude one-time adjustments you cannot explain. You already have your ownership share in
        that payment; do not multiply it by your royalty decimal again.
      </p>
      <p>
        The rate and horizon starting values below are editable teaching assumptions, not
        recommended rates for your property. No result appears until you enter your income and
        calculate.
      </p>
      <form id="income-form">
        <div class="fields">
          <label
            >Average monthly royalty income paid to you ($)<input
              name="monthlyIncome"
              type="number"
              min="0"
              max="1000000000"
              step="0.01"
              required
              inputmode="decimal"
              aria-describedby="income-help"
            /></label
          >
          <label>Statement period ending<input name="recordsDate" type="date" required /></label>
          <label
            >Assumed annual income decline (%)<input
              name="declinePercent"
              type="number"
              value="10"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              step="0.1"
              required
            /></label
          >
          <label
            >Assumed annual discount rate (%)<input
              name="discountPercent"
              type="number"
              value="10"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              step="0.1"
              required
            /></label
          >
          <label
            >Years to model<input
              name="years"
              type="number"
              value="10"
              min="1"
              max="30"
              step="1"
              required
            /></label
          >
        </div>
        <p id="income-help">
          No producing income or missing statements? Leave this calculation unused. That does not
          mean the mineral interest has no value.
        </p>
        <button type="submit">Calculate my income scenarios</button>
        <button type="reset" class="secondary">Clear this calculation</button>
      </form>
      <div id="income-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
      <details>
        <summary>See the formula and what it leaves out</summary>
        <p>
          Year t income = monthly income × 12 × (1 − decline rate)<sup>t−1</sup>. Present value =
          the sum of each modeled year's income ÷ (1 + discount rate)<sup>t</sup>. Year one uses a
          full year at your starting income; payments are discounted at each year end.
        </p>
        <p>
          This simplified constant-decline model includes no terminal value, undeveloped acreage,
          future wells or lease bonus. It holds prices and deductions within your starting income
          assumption. It does not forecast engineering reserves, seasonal payments, taxes, buyer
          costs or lease/title changes. The discount rate reflects an assumption about timing and
          risk; it is not a promised investment return.
        </p>
        <p>
          The comparison cases change decline by 10 percentage points and discount by 5 percentage
          points, bounded between 0 and 100. They illustrate sensitivity, not a confidence interval
          or a sale-price range. Buyers may use different records, forecasts and commercial
          assumptions.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="acreage-heading">
      <h2 id="acreage-heading">Compare the acreage basis of a written offer.</h2>
      <p>
        Use gross tract acres and your documented fractional <strong>mineral ownership</strong>. Net
        mineral acres and net royalty acres are different measures. A division-order payment decimal
        or a lease royalty rate is not your mineral ownership fraction.
      </p>
      <form id="acreage-form">
        <div class="fields">
          <label
            >Gross acres in the described tract<input
              name="grossAcres"
              type="number"
              min="0.000001"
              max="1000000000"
              step="any"
              required
            /></label
          >
          <label
            >Your mineral ownership share (%)<input
              name="ownershipPercent"
              type="number"
              min="0.000001"
              max="100"
              step="any"
              required
              aria-describedby="ownership-help"
            /></label
          >
          <label
            >Total written offer for this same interest ($)<input
              name="offer"
              type="number"
              min="0"
              max="1000000000000"
              step="0.01"
              required
            /></label
          >
          <label>Offer date<input name="offerDate" type="date" required /></label>
        </div>
        <p id="ownership-help">
          For example, a documented 1/4 mineral interest is 25%. If the basis is unknown, ask for
          the controlling records rather than guessing.
        </p>
        <button type="submit">Compare my offer basis</button><button type="reset" class="secondary"
          >Clear this comparison</button
        >
      </form>
      <div id="acreage-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
      <p>
        Formula: gross acres × mineral ownership share = estimated net mineral acres. Written offer
        ÷ those acres = the offer per net mineral acre. This standardizes your stated inputs; it
        does not establish fair price or that the offer covers the same rights, depths and
        conditions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="landman-heading">
      <h2 id="landman-heading">What a landman checks before a purchase.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>What is actually owned?</strong> Legal description, chain of title, probate, reservations,
          depths and mineral versus royalty interest.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What is being conveyed?</strong> Match the offer, agreement, deed and exhibits. Clarify
          retained rights and effective dates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What supports the income?</strong> Lease terms, division orders, payment history, deductions,
          operator and available production records. Engineering forecasts and local market evidence may
          be needed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What could change the price?</strong> Ask which quantities and title assumptions are
          preliminary, what adjustments are allowed and what records must support them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What makes closing possible?</strong> Identify the buyer, signer, funding party, review
          deadline, extension rules and payment/release sequence.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Landmen, engineers, valuation professionals and attorneys have different roles. An online
        calculation cannot substitute for their property-specific work. <a
          href="https://www.landman.org/articles/Vol_61.5_-_PAULA_FLEMING_-_Divestiture_and_Acquisition_-_Due_Diligence_101_for_Land_Professionals_.PDF"
          >AAPL due-diligence guidance</a
        > · <a
          href="https://naro-us.org/learn/top-10-mineral-owner-questions/mineral-rights-valuation-guide"
          >NARO valuation methods</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h3>If the offer drops, ask for the explanation in writing.</h3>
      <p>
        Compare the original and revised amount, interest, acreage, conditions and dates. Request
        the calculation and supporting records. A documented ownership adjustment can be legitimate;
        an unexplained reduction, newly introduced condition or pressure to sign deserves further
        questions. Do not assume either deception or fairness from a number alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/guides/mineral-rights-offer-comparison-worksheet.pdf" download
          >Download the fillable comparison worksheets</a
        >, record what is unresolved, and <a href="/book/"
          >book a free educational conversation with a human underwriter</a
        >. Elena is the fictional AI scheduling guide; she helps arrange the appointment.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-note">
        Calculations run in your browser. Calculator inputs are not submitted to MRX. Refreshing or
        leaving the page clears them; save your own notes if you want to discuss the assumptions.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
  import { modelIncome, compareAcreage } from '../lib/mineral-rights-scenarios';
  const money = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {
    style: 'currency',
    currency: 'USD',
    maximumFractionDigits: 0,
  });
  const number = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 4 });
  const getNumber = (data: FormData, key: string) => {
    const value = String(data.get(key) ?? '').trim();
    if (!value) throw new Error('Complete the labeled inputs before calculating.');
    return Number(value);
  };
  function output(id: string, text: string) {
    const el = document.getElementById(id)!;
    el.replaceChildren();
    el.hidden = false;
    const p = document.createElement('p');
    p.textContent = text;
    el.append(p);
    el.focus();
    return el;
  }
  const income = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#income-form')!;
  income.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (!income.reportValidity()) return;
    try {
      const data = new FormData(income);
      const base = {
        monthlyIncome: getNumber(data, 'monthlyIncome'),
        declinePercent: getNumber(data, 'declinePercent'),
        discountPercent: getNumber(data, 'discountPercent'),
        years: getNumber(data, 'years'),
      };
      const result = modelIncome(base);
      const conservative = modelIncome({
        ...base,
        declinePercent: Math.min(100, base.declinePercent + 10),
        discountPercent: Math.min(100, base.discountPercent + 5),
      });
      const higher = modelIncome({
        ...base,
        declinePercent: Math.max(0, base.declinePercent - 10),
        discountPercent: Math.max(0, base.discountPercent - 5),
      });
      const el = output(
        'income-result',
        `Your ${base.years}-year modeled present value of income: ${money.format(result.presentValue)}. This is not market value, an appraisal or an offer. Statement period ending ${data.get('recordsDate')}; starting monthly income ${money.format(base.monthlyIncome)}, annual decline ${base.declinePercent}%, discount ${base.discountPercent}%.`,
      );
      const p = document.createElement('p');
      p.textContent = `Sensitivity examples: higher decline and discount ${money.format(conservative.presentValue)}; lower decline and discount ${money.format(higher.presentValue)}. Undiscounted income in your base scenario: ${money.format(result.undiscountedIncome)}. No income or value after year ${base.years} is included.`;
      el.append(p);
      const details = document.createElement('details');
      const summary = document.createElement('summary');
      summary.textContent = 'Show the annual calculation';
      details.append(summary);
      const list = document.createElement('ol');
      result.rows.forEach((row) => {
        const li = document.createElement('li');
        li.textContent = `Year ${row.year}: income ${money.format(row.cashFlow)}; discounted income ${money.format(row.presentValue)}.`;
        list.append(li);
      });
      details.append(list);
      el.append(details);
    } catch (error) {
      output(
        'income-result',
        error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Check your inputs and try again.',
      );
    }
  });
  const acreage = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#acreage-form')!;
  acreage.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (!acreage.reportValidity()) return;
    try {
      const data = new FormData(acreage);
      const gross = getNumber(data, 'grossAcres');
      const share = getNumber(data, 'ownershipPercent');
      const offer = getNumber(data, 'offer');
      const result = compareAcreage(gross, share, offer);
      output(
        'acreage-result',
        `${number.format(gross)} gross acres × ${number.format(share)}% mineral ownership = ${number.format(result.netMineralAcres)} estimated net mineral acres. Your ${money.format(offer)} written offer dated ${data.get('offerDate')} equals ${money.format(result.offerPerNetMineralAcre)} per net mineral acre on these stated inputs. This does not verify ownership, equal terms or fair market price.`,
      );
    } catch (error) {
      output(
        'acreage-result',
        error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Check your inputs and try again.',
      );
    }
  });
  for (const [form, id] of [
    [income, 'income-result'],
    [acreage, 'acreage-result'],
  ] as const) {
    form.addEventListener('reset', () => {
      const el = document.getElementById(id)!;
      el.hidden = true;
      el.replaceChildren();
    });
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      const el = document.getElementById(id)!;
      el.hidden = true;
      el.replaceChildren();
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .calculator {
    max-width: 980px;
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.3rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #cbd5df;
  }
  p,
  li {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  li {
    margin-block: 0.7rem;
  }
  .fields {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.2rem;
  }
  label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  input {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid #526878;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font: inherit;
    color: #112b40;
    background: white;
  }
  button {
    margin: 0.7rem 0.5rem 0.7rem 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.1rem;
    min-height: 48px;
    background: #112b40;
    color: white;
    border: 2px solid #112b40;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .secondary {
    background: white;
    color: #112b40;
  }
  :is(a, button, input, summary):focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #bc8b31;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  [role='status'] {
    margin-block: 1rem;
    background: #f7f4ed;
    padding: 1rem;
    border-left: 4px solid #bc8b31;
  }
  details {
    margin-block: 1rem;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-block: 0.6rem;
  }
  .privacy-note {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .fields {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    button {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
